Subject: [PATCH] Support explicit ECom plugin identities in native DLL conversion

Apply after patches 0001 through 0005 to symbian-platform v0.3.0.
Add a DLL-only --uid2 option and ConvertDllWithUid2 API for the original
ECom plugin identity. Ordinary DLL UID2 0x1000008d remains the default;
explicit plugin UID2 0x10009d8d accepts a nonzero assigned UID3. Existing
ConvertDll ABI, EXE identity policy, capability mask and CRC validation remain.

FEP identity is established by EKA's preserved avkonfep_general.mmp and native
artifact (UID2 0x10009d8d / UID3 0x100056de); no header postprocessing is used.
The original production source retains its licensing. The changes and added
host GTest follow symbian-platform's Apache-2.0 license. The test extends the
SDK's existing bounded ELF fixture; no firmware or third-party implementation
code is included in this patch.

Six native identity tests join symbian_e32_test, which the existing WebKit
build-symbian-native.sh builds and runs when SYMBIAN_NATIVE_TESTS=ON (default).
This portable patch omits machine-local .dev experiment notes. It has the
same three production file bytes and test code as the earlier external
62-test / 13-CLI-check evidence. No new portable host rebuild is claimed.

diff --git a/cpp/symbian/e32/e32.cc b/cpp/symbian/e32/e32.cc
